    ],
    "description": "How the WFM authenticates the caller: every Management Interface endpoint refuses a request without a client certificate; the client SVID must chain to the Trust Bundle through CA certificates (a self-signed substitute and a leaf signed by an SVID are refused); a validly issued SVID of another wfm-id is refused (NOT RUN unless that SVID is placed in the cert folder); and forged RFC 9440 Client-Cert / Client-Cert-Chain headers never authenticate a request.",
